<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n112565" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῠλία</span></b> , poet. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῡλετ-ίη</span></b> , ἡ, a tree mentioned
		with the olive in <i><span class="en">
			Od.
			5.477
		</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δοιοὺς . . θάμνους, ἐξ ὁμόθεν
			πεφυῶτασ—ὁ μὲν φυλίης, ὁ δ᾽ ἐλαίης</span>), apptly.
		(cf. Sch.ad loc., <i><span class="en">
			Hsch.
		</span></i>) a kind of <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>wild
			olive,</i> but distd. fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κότινος</span>
			and said to be Troezenian by <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				2.32.10
			</span></i> (written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φυλλία</span>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Gym.</u>
				43
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				5.474
			</span></i>; wrongly identified by <i><span class="en">
				Ammon.
				<u>Diff.</u>
				p.135V.
			</span></i> with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σχῖνος.</span></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
